ttps://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/snoodleboot","id":10266249,"login":"snoodleboot","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMjY2MjQ5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/snoodleboot-io/lavs-core/commits/59926c188e854224a96ddde632a44dda35e04363/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T02:43:06Z","email":"John.aven.phd@gmail.com","name":"John Aven"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T02:43:06Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: reconcile branch-naming rules with actual practice (LAV-67) (#72)\n\nCONTRIBUTING.md told contributors to use `feature/BRANCH_NAME` and\n`bug/BUG_NAME`, but the project does not name branches that way. Of the head\nbranches behind the last 40 merged PRs, 19 are `feat/` and 5 `bugfix/`,\nagainst 5 `feature/` and 1 `bug/` — and those outliers are the recent PRs that\nfollowed this file as written (#67, #69, #70, #71). Because the documented form\nhas no ticket slot, none of them carried a ticket id.\n\nRewrite the section to the form the project practices:\n`{type}/{ticket}-{description}` with `feat/`, `bugfix/` or `hotfix/`.\n\n`{ticket}` accepts a GitHub issue number as well as a Linear key. This file is\nread by outside contributors, who can open a GitHub issue but have no Linear\naccess, so a Linear-only rule would be unusable for exactly its audience.","tree":{"sha":"4fa3be940040ae7dbbb2682e13a04dae3f5f5586","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/snoodleboot-io/lavs-core/git/trees/4fa3be940040ae7dbbb2682e13a04dae3f5f5586"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/snoodleboot-io/lavs-core/git/commits/59926c188e854224a96ddde632a44dda35e04363","verification":{"payload":"tree 4fa3be940040ae7dbbb2682e13a04dae3f5f5586\nparent 927f48b699d0bcbf45ff24cb88af69e5fdb7ad08\nauthor John Aven <John.aven.phd@gmail.com> 1789267386 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789267386 -0500\n\ndocs: reconcile branch-naming rules with actual practice (LAV-67) (#72)\n\nCONTRIBUTING.md told contributors to use `feature/BRANCH_NAME` and\n`bug/BUG_NAME`, but the project does not name branches that way. Of the head\nbranches behind the last 40 merged PRs, 19 are `feat/` and 5 `bugfix/`,\nagainst 5 `feature/` and 1 `bug/` — and those outliers are the recent PRs that\nfollowed this file as written (#67, #69, #70, #71). Because the documented form\nhas no ticket slot, none of them carried a ticket id.\n\nRewrite the section to the form the project practices:\n`{type}/{ticket}-{description}` with `feat/`, `bugfix/` or `hotfix/`.\n\n`{ticket}` accepts a GitHub issue number as well as a Linear key. This file is\nread by outside contributors, who can open a GitHub issue but have no Linear\naccess, so a Linear-only rule would be unusable for exactly its audience.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqpg26CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAgXAQAKZpV/3Fo0rqhIEnIINiqdzN\nU9/Kv47snaMCJG9NNskwd1VNfSnjrJqqJcJ+APeloz3e8YkDKslC3t8PqM86a23H\n02KuwfAvmTWvFw7Xahtp05PRDeh82A/gzewnmNV97fXgu5/qmnsjhfpIOKvIp/Lf\n3rdoj0nsFxsFUqC4tDKo2jBJRQp14caf4Cd/l+YFdFjXVuphXGl6Y6sPt7+jV6+s\ntSDeGX56tgipNeLDCnwNzEF6aA2ix/fWg3jM6uOms3k8i8lfYsdZRhlRyFfdYmGz\ntBplkntAKcdRmcFQ/RobaJawgmnwLK+zMTlexFzv1jVDqHs2GnD+lIabaM+kI/TT\nd5+Swu80Do4elhmS1eVZqmFg2bCF