r_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/snoodleboot","id":10266249,"login":"snoodleboot","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMjY2MjQ5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/snoodleboot-io/lavs-core/commits/b0bea4edf2637259d6e60aafdcef85ea3d25bece/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-23T06:39:31Z","email":"John.aven.phd@gmail.com","name":"John Aven"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T06:39:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(ui): derived-bump readout, per-version change levels, dependency SSE (LAV-63) (#69)\n\n(a) Derived-bump readout\n- formatBumpRationale shapes the wire''s opaque JSON string into one human\n  line at a single boundary, falling back to the raw string on malformed or\n  unrecognised payloads rather than dropping it. The wire type stays\n  `string | null` everywhere upstream.\n- The readout badges the LATEST CUT release''s bump (▲ + the level in words)\n  and shows the shaped rationale, but only while the meridian sits at \"now\".\n  The derived version is scrub-derived and the bump is frozen, so rendering\n  both off \"now\" would let one card contradict itself.\n\n(b) Per-component change_level\n- Joined by version_id, not component_id: a `ReleaseComponent` carries both,\n  and the meridian scrubs through history, so keying by component would paint\n  the latest release''s level onto a scrubbed-back version. Only the pinned\n  station badges, only when its version is in the latest release, and an\n  active selection''s impact badge takes the slot.\n\n(c) Dependency SSE\n- dependency.added / dependency.removed ride the existing product stream,\n  parsed with the same guard as version.created. Pure reducers fold them into\n  the GRAPH cache, then the graph key is invalidated: REST GET /graph stays\n  authoritative, so a dropped or duplicated frame re-syncs.\n\nFakeEventSource gains emitRaw so the malformed-frame test can deliver an\nunparseable body without reaching into private state.","tree":{"sha":"cd184695bd7f236ec67cc211075aa98f16b1c03e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/snoodleboot-io/lavs-core/git/trees/cd184695bd7f236ec67cc211075aa98f16b1c03e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/snoodleboot-io/lavs-core/git/commits/b0bea4edf2637259d6e60aafdcef85ea3d25bece","verification":{"payload":"tree cd184695bd7f236ec67cc211075aa98f16b1c03e\nparent 1fa3b22bb367d11403d7c3f3cdf8cba7b272d3eb\nauthor John Aven <John.aven.phd@gmail.com> 1787467171 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787467171 -0500\n\nfeat(ui): derived-bump readout, per-version change levels, dependency SSE (LAV-63) (#69)\n\n(a) Derived-bump readout\n- formatBumpRationale shapes the wire''s opaque JSON string into one human\n  line at a single boundary, falling back to the raw string on malformed or\n  unrecognised payloads rather than dropping it. The wire type stays\n  `string | null` everywhere upstream.\n- The readout badges the LATEST CUT release''s bump (▲ + the level in words)\n  and shows the shaped rationale, but only while the meridian sits at \"now\".\n  The derived version is scrub-derived and the bump is frozen, so rendering\n  both off \"now\" would let one card contradict itself.\n\n(b) Per-component change_level\n- Joined by version_id, not component_id: a `ReleaseComponent` carries both,\n  and the meridian scrubs through history, so keying by component would paint\n  the latest release''s level onto a scrubbed-back version. Only the pinned\n  station badges, only when its version is in the latest release, and an\n  active selection''s impact badge takes the slot.\n\n(c) Dependency SSE\n- dependency.added / dependency.removed ride the existing product stream,\n  parsed with the same guard as version.created. Pure reducers fold them into\n  the GRAPH cache, then the graph key is invalidated: REST GET /graph stays\n  authoritative, so a dropped or duplicated frame re-syncs.\n\nFakeEventSource gains emitRaw so the malformed-frame test can deliver an\nunparseable body without reaching into private state.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqipWjCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAvesQAJub1FhmkmcNZEKgbeRccLDd\nLYjrym7EszB6v54KDgTpD841kFJGPAzsuNVVP+vk4uiqX/omt3h9BS+HPMzIHmWv\nCksl/CbqrTUCU5lL4ZG13nWoO3Ju6qSjnDh+BihzD8jaD5uhSk/BvRXDiKoRPrIu\nowQeJK+yBXDYXBkV2GYALJpfGhyuCbXewXAdGQ2ooQVPwgXRLAnDEJ01Yi9dtUdQ\nd/Q0pZglyNSbK3+mzaYO/9OJbBd4dv7Z2b/Dzd8WYTNrpBpsRk7iDvnVf6TK3vMb\nxU4Y9c3vQOYn/K8Iq2p3aGr4BHRSjldr59pGW8psEYj3TpC7T1yvGWqXPakiasqe\n7d07A51hM7Fm3M+3yEwGcuh79eCAWfLHSvMd6OevjnL7OxgV+PTyW/2HRhqIK2Kr\noLMRwCeQMXoQT/YCBNqnBNjD9OlG5UWXc6+8wZd4htVdmOm1xv9JpRKjrcF/MmiF\naR/139vOdrpqBecblzWsCDsqxBbi5a8aW+MaMPAZRBGOpvpHLibwHGc023bedksw\n8FgUAdiHCfr/ws5g+WWv0bnRCx2kD8jFuRNPyi6sjKuGfRamhJ+lQJOuEcNPxp0u\n/qDK62nTNXHZEuSP4weUTz6YFrGfA37j/uoTs72cqLm73QYux7beKuwlxQNiksRx\nPC3Sm92uM15e9zaLZ3K2\n=tzSU\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-23T06:39:31Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/snoodleboot-io/lavs-core/commit/b0bea4edf2637259d6e60aafdcef85ea3d25bece","node_id":"C_kwDON50rGNoAKGIwYmVhNGVkZjI2MzcyNTlkNmU2MGFhZmRjZWY4NWVhM2QyNWJlY2U","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/snoodleboot-io/lavs-core/commit/1fa3b22bb367d11403d7c3f3cdf8cba7b272d3eb","sha":"1fa3b22bb367d11403d7c3f3cdf8cba7b272d3eb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/snoodleboot-io/lavs-core/commits/1fa3b22bb367d11403d7c3f3cdf8cba7b272d3eb"}],"sha":"b0bea4edf2637259d6e60aafdcef85ea3d25bece","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/snoodleboot-io/lavs-core/commits/b0bea4edf2637259d6e60aafdcef85ea3d25bece"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10266249?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/snoodleboot","id":10266249,"login":"snoodleboot","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMjY2MjQ5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/snoodleboot-io/lavs-core/commits/1fa3b22bb367d11403d7c3f3cdf8cba7b272d3eb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-23T06:36:57Z","email":"John.aven.phd@gmail.com","name":"John Aven"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T06:36:57Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(ui): impact highlight for the Constellation (LAV-62) (#70)\n\nSelecting a component lights its blast radius from GET /impact.\n\n- useImpact(productId, componentId) fires only on a selection and holds a\n  30s staleTime so hovering never re-fetches.\n- Lane labels become keyboard-first toggles: role=button, tabIndex, and\n  aria-pressed, so the selection is exposed programmatically and never\n  colour-only. Escape clears it; re-selecting toggles it off; the label\n  stops pointer propagation so a click can never start a meridian scrub.\n- Impact keys on COMPONENT id and lands on the PINNED station only — one\n  badge and one aria annotation per impacted lane, never one per version\n  node. Dependents are tinted by projected level with a ▲ glyph plus the\n  level in words, the source gets a dashed ring, the rest dim, and an edge\n  brightens only when both its ends sit in the blast radius.\n- The glow runs through the useReducedMotion JS seam rather than a\n  jsdom-inert CSS @media, so the reduced-motion assertion is a real test.","tree":{"sha":"83e0b7fc373071121fa3bc0033bb65407ea6013d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/snoodleboot-io/lavs-core/git/trees/83e0b7fc373071121fa3bc0033bb65407ea6013d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/snoodleboot-io/lavs-core/git/commits/1fa3b22bb367d11403d7c3f3cdf8cba7b272d3eb","verification":{"payload":"tree 83e0b7fc373071121fa3bc0033bb65407ea6013d\nparent 2bb462d96211025d050d1dd6f61ca3b9949947cc\nauthor John Aven <John.aven.phd@gmail.com> 1787467017 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787467017 -0500\n\nfeat(ui): impact highlight for the Constellation (LAV-62) (#70)\n\nSelecting a component lights its blast radius from GET /impact.\n\n- useImpact(productId, componentId) fires only on a selection and holds a\n  30s staleTime so hovering never re-fetches.\n- Lane labels become keyboard-first toggles: role=button, tabIndex, and\n  aria-pressed, so the selection is exposed programmatically and never\n  colour-only. Escape clears it; re-selecting toggles it off; the label\n  stops pointer propagation so a click can never start a meridian scrub.\n- Impact keys on COMPONENT id and lands on the PINNED station only — one\n  badge and one aria annotation per impacted lane, never one per version\n  node. Dependents are tinted by projected level with a ▲ glyph plus the\n  level in words, the source gets a dashed ring, the rest dim, and an edge\n  brightens only when both its ends sit in the blast radius.\n- The glow runs through the useReducedMotion JS seam rather than a\n  jsdom-inert CSS @media, so the reduced-motion assertion is a real test.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqipUJCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAs8AQAATgzOGPmaXwyWYffkDcPU9h\n1hK2LgLbT656Lx3Azl1btgtblY63cAvPoX/ZqJ2SdBa5kMvCzqaN+Gq+7dt4NDdl\nnlUxi0M1e41u3blCFqTQhcxwJnp53iutOYLUxHjq3oI6iX/LugEyRclTgCiZzEVj\np7uj3lt+tT364F1JaKeSXiPSvHZi42dt2lTtaIYYDpsxo0yLK8I48l7DAGshSs+C\nnSsuZJF33GeZneTPaX30NPQL2KPJG9DkjFhhKJIGlyeCeBZ8kXlp5YIXeAp9YhK5\ngF8636iUBn1zOkCry/Mmgp9T1hhnot0uZqEiWkTlWiEq0fiROx9pcm4oLe2CRwZ9\n2wGK9JZsE0GX/BtCtd6dYFR3O64b5FOp33b+IXXzqhobAA/hGPP1SZklv0rSps/j\n8yY28jFJXgbvO+PA1dJuJzA3oRIkCMoxy39tlbmiAgTQ7N4BHadwNIaaYaM8tUgL\nZedVCVFuaFIZiy75corjjgYaZhG+BWgPiBNOo/AkXUFlmMqvEdsWVYaVomxxxDRH\n+SlYm6XQnQnfQde89dYqduVOoeYosqgjvzyDZKmPJx1UaDm1iIr56Ig0sUk0CxTj\nyJv7X+ijjcmETsDDSuUVOadsaDYZOTKSylziR/RzxOVeXWzokNjMh9RnYfOssxKl\nRSYp0Skfrcn2jR1qYnrK\n=dH/B\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-23T06:36:57Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","fol