d1dd6f61ca3b9949947cc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10266249?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/snoodleboot","id":10266249,"login":"snoodleboot","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMjY2MjQ5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/snoodleboot-io/lavs-core/commits/7e4ce03947ec30e90a8e84f3f4658864aad0d2ee/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-23T03:39:15Z","email":"John.aven.phd@gmail.com","name":"John Aven"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T03:39:15Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(p9): product dependency graphs — intra-product DAG + derived versions (#65) (#66)\n\n* docs(p9): add dependency-graph execution plan (#65)\n\nFirst v2 phase (P8 = v1 hardening is already taken). Intra-product component\ndependency DAG + cut-time change derivation that replaces the blind minor-bump,\ngated behind a per-product bump_policy so existing products are unchanged.\n\n* feat(p9): add dependency-graph schema foundation (#65)\n\nAdd the component_dependencies edge table across all four dialects\n(DuckDB/PostgreSQL/MySQL/SQL Server), the BumpLevel enum, and the derived-bump\ncolumns (releases.bump_level/bump_rationale, release_components.change_level,\nproducts.bump_policy DEFAULT ''legacy''). Product-scoped unique edge key; app-layer\ncycle/self/cross guards (no recursive CTE). Existing-table column upgrade for the\nnetworked backends is deferred to F-4, mirroring the base_version precedent.\n\n* feat(p9): add pure change classifier + DAG bump derivation (#65)\n\nchange_classifier classifies a component''s own change (added=MINOR, removed\nhandled by the caller, prerelease-only=PATCH, regression by highest differing\nposition). bump_propagation walks the intra-product DAG with a contraction-only\npolicy so the product bump equals the max own change (edges drive per-component\nrationale/impact, not the version). product_version gains bump_major/bump_patch/\napply_bump. All pure and DB-free.\n\n* feat(p9): add dependency edge CRUD + graph endpoints (#65)\n\nPOST/DELETE /products/{id}/dependencies and GET /products/{id}/graph, backed by a\ncomponent_dependencies query lane. App-layer guards reject self-edges (409),\ncross-product endpoints (409), duplicates (409), cycles (409, pure reachability\ncheck), and missing product/component (404). No recursive CTE.\n\n* feat(p9): derive release bump from component changes + policy dispatch (#65)\n\nCutReleaseQuery now reads products.bump_policy: legacy forces the pre-P9 minor\nbump (byte-identical); default classifies each active component against the prior\nmanifest, walks the dependency graph, and takes the graph-wide max. Persists\nbump_level + JSON bump_rationale on the release and per-component change_level,\nthreaded through the cut mapper and both read paths (nullable, so pre-P9 rows\nread back). New products are created with the default policy; acceptance tests\nupdated to the derived contract (a real component change drives the bump; a\nno-change re-cut derives NONE and repeats the version).\n\n* feat(p9): add GET /impact what-if endpoint (#65)\n\nProjects a hypothetical major change to a component across its transitive\ndependents, reusing the propagation engine, and lists each impacted dependent\nwith its projected change level. Read-only; 404 for unknown product/component.\n\n* feat(p9): emit dependency.added/removed SSE events (#65)\n\nAdd EventType.DEPENDENCY_ADDED/REMOVED; AddDependencyQuery and RemoveDependencyQuery\ntake an optional EventBus and publish a product-scoped event after the mutation,\nmirroring create_version_query. Wired through the products router. (bump_level\nalready rides release.cut via the release model.)\n\n* test(p9): 4-backend parity for the component_dependencies edge table (#65)\n\nRaw parameterized inserts (bypassing the app guard) prove, on real PostgreSQL,\nMySQL and SQL Server: the table exists with resolvable FKs; a duplicate\n(product_id, from, to) is rejected by the DB''s own UNIQUE key; and the same\nfrom/to under two products both succeed (product_id is part of the key).\n\n* docs(p9): document the dependency graph + derived versions (#65)\n\nAPI_CONTRACT: dependency/graph/impact endpoints, bump_level/bump_rationale/\nchange_level on releases, dependency SSE events, the derived-bump contract\n(a no-change re-cut derives none), and a new section 10. ROADMAP: v2 north\nstar, the P9 phase row/detail, and the P10 cross-product outline.\n\n* test(p9): update release-parity second-cut to the derived contract (#65)\n\nUnder the default policy a no-change re-cut derives none, so the three backend\nrelease-parity ''second cut bumps minor'' tests now make a real minor component\nchange between cuts to drive the bump. Matches the acceptance-test update.","tree":{"sha":"2e255eadc42e1c862b34886ba14b7103092e64d5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/snoodleboot-io/lavs-core/git/trees/2e255eadc42e1c862b34886ba14b7103092e64d5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/snoodleboot-io/lavs-core/git/commits/7e4ce03947ec30e90a8e84f3f4658864aad0d2ee","verification":{"payload":"tree 2e255eadc42e1c862b34886ba14b7103092e64d5\nparent eea01714bc01f4aaccd87142cc4a02bf7ceb401a\nauthor John Ave