 now reads products.bump_policy: legacy forces the pre-P9 minor\nbump (byte-identical); default classifies each active component against the prior\nmanifest, walks the dependency graph, and takes the graph-wide max. Persists\nbump_level + JSON bump_rationale on the release and per-component change_level,\nthreaded through the cut mapper and both read paths (nullable, so pre-P9 rows\nread back). New products are created with the default policy; acceptance tests\nupdated to the derived contract (a real component change drives the bump; a\nno-change re-cut derives NONE and repeats the version).\n\n* feat(p9): add GET /impact what-if endpoint (#65)\n\nProjects a hypothetical major change to a component across its transitive\ndependents, reusing the propagation engine, and lists each impacted dependent\nwith its projected change level. Read-only; 404 for unknown product/component.\n\n* feat(p9): emit dependency.added/removed SSE events (#65)\n\nAdd EventType.DEPENDENCY_ADDED/REMOVED; AddDependencyQuery and RemoveDependencyQuery\ntake an optional EventBus and publish a product-scoped event after the mutation,\nmirroring create_version_query. Wired through the products router. (bump_level\nalready rides release.cut via the release model.)\n\n* test(p9): 4-backend parity for the component_dependencies edge table (#65)\n\nRaw parameterized inserts (bypassing the app guard) prove, on real PostgreSQL,\nMySQL and SQL Server: the table exists with resolvable FKs; a duplicate\n(product_id, from, to) is rejected by the DB''s own UNIQUE key; and the same\nfrom/to under two products both succeed (product_id is part of the key).\n\n* docs(p9): document the dependency graph + derived versions (#65)\n\nAPI_CONTRACT: dependency/graph/impact endpoints, bump_level/bump_rationale/\nchange_level on releases, dependency SSE events, the derived-bump contract\n(a no-change re-cut derives none), and a new section 10. ROADMAP: v2 north\nstar, the P9 phase row/detail, and the P10 cross-product outline.\n\n* test(p9): update release-parity second-cut to the derived contract (#65)\n\nUnder the default policy a no-change re-cut derives none, so the three backend\nrelease-parity ''second cut bumps minor'' tests now make a real minor component\nchange between cuts to drive the bump. Matches the acceptance-test update.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqimtjCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAnFAQAAd5nShGxTdVaMXOPTmLAT9B\nk7Ef9+4jJtAxL1QAGh2dOQnkplYml0Rp+Wqo8XhjS4AzISWlMWT7LgajRCQX8X8u\nBFzKGNiY/SuaCBhnYuy5ozItmKxq+ls0/Hk1D2+cZuRJggs337hNFMLq3j5OUFzd\nAXUDDKxTy/OB4NfMpTbPeLN1r03onyY1C/hYQFFGPSyhrtyUUZPKehlm/evvV2b9\n7dKAM4gApC0NYp+yJxadPdKMkYnJxlZjrDREE6GjDDvnolsYLEDLngoPBl9QyLWL\nwOC7ahgZ8tzMSoPiC8hvCdDmeIVtmgash1RAkLKEKXbdzH/Pj1PmOngAfGbzyLlj\n3sZsukFpwGGas9heu6PVHGQIrF3uLo+YcRbPnmv4UOtUS3AHFCniruhhn3LPwLAw\ngshj15P2efkVnzDPNipZ+hJ/Q4yLrOjeCQ3zp9TvUu8Utr5H32QmXLqfOixHZI2M\nC6SZz584i8LcLQ2kyj+jITLuMXfx3e2DrAoeWs/Npyr8gjV0XmEUAugAPgLDdvjI\nLzNrGDZhmXCE8ZCaMyVMdwPrIqHdd7D3W13yNyOl++viGSjbCC+QpfYP+UI/EZvi\nfiwx+ph67WCNNaUAn1yxEmWGdzJnk26YNC8BG/EW19nlJ22Ws3QuvNYVScqCPkhM\nSm9wiI0pRL0vVXhF87HS\n=u/k4\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-23T03:39:16Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/o