":"John Aven"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-22T22:21:27Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(repo): untrack the agent config and fix the broken README link (#53) (#62)\n\nTwo repo-hygiene fixes that only touch tracked-file metadata and docs.\n\n**Untrack the agent config.** `.claude/` (115 files) and `.prompticorn/` (4) were\ntracked and publicly browsable. They are developer tooling, not product source,\nand are now shared from the workspace root so one copy serves lavs-core, lavs-ee\nand lavs-site. `git rm --cached` untracks while leaving every file on disk, so\nlocal agent discovery is unaffected — this is metadata-only.\n\nNote `.prompticorn/` was *already* listed in .gitignore, but its files had been\ncommitted before that rule existed. .gitignore does not untrack what is already\ntracked, so the rule was inert and those session files stayed public. `.claude/`\njoins it, and both are now genuinely excluded.\n\n**Fix the broken public README link.** The EE extraction moved\n`docs/ops/STYTCH_MANUAL_SMOKE.md` into the private lavs-ee repo and left\n`docs/ops/` empty here, so the OSS README pointed at a 404. The prose stays; the\ndead link is replaced with a reference to the EE distribution. Every other\nrelative link in the README was checked and resolves.\n\n**CLAUDE.md is annotated rather than moved.** It is tracked and makes 27\nreferences into `.claude/`, so untracking alone would leave a public file\npointing at paths that no longer exist — the same defect being fixed in the\nREADME. Moving it was outside what was agreed, so instead it carries a short note\nexplaining that the tree lives at the workspace root, that discovery walks up to\nfind it, and that the references will not resolve in a bare clone by design.\n\nThe archived `docs/planning/P*_MULTIAGENT_EXECUTION_PLAN.md` files also reference\n`.claude/` paths. Those are historical records of how the work was executed and\nwere accurate when written, so they are left alone.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"651b5dc691eced59ea0befaecfd62293610690cf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/snoodleboot-io/lavs-core/git/trees/651b5dc691eced59ea0befaecfd62293610690cf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/snoodleboot-io/lavs-core/git/commits/eea01714bc01f4aaccd87142cc4a02bf7ceb401a","verification":{"payload":"tree 651b5dc691eced59ea0befaecfd62293610690cf\nparent fac5b305641ec9072b27068a61a38656a50a4436\nauthor John Aven <John.aven.phd@gmail.com> 1787437287 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787437287 -0700\n\nchore(repo): untrack the agent config and fix the broken README link (#53) (#62)\n\nTwo repo-hygiene fixes that only touch tracked-file metadata and docs.\n\n**Untrack the agent config.** `.claude/` (115 files) and `.prompticorn/` (4) were\ntracked and publicly browsable. They are developer tooling, not product source,\nand are now shared from the workspace root so one copy serves lavs-core, lavs-ee\nand lavs-site. `git rm --cached` untracks while leaving every file on disk, so\nlocal agent discovery is unaffected — this is metadata-only.\n\nNote `.prompticorn/` was *already* listed in .gitignore, but its files had been\ncommitted before that rule existed. .gitignore does not untrack what is already\ntracked, so the rule was inert and those session files stayed public. `.claude/`\njoins it, and both are now genuinely excluded.\n\n**Fix the broken public README link.** The EE extraction moved\n`docs/ops/STYTCH_MANUAL_SMOKE.md` into the private lavs-ee repo and left\n`docs/ops/` empty here, so the OSS README pointed at a 404. The prose stays; the\ndead link is replaced with a reference to the EE distribution. Every other\nrelative link in the README was checked and resolves.\n\n**CLAUDE.md is annotated rather than moved.** It is tracked and makes 27\nreferences into `.claude/`, so untracking alone would leave a public file\npointing at paths that no longer exist — the same defect being fixed in the\nREADME. Moving it was outside what was agreed, so instead it carries a short note\nexplaining that the tree lives at the workspace root, that discovery walks up to\nfind it, and that the references will not resolve in a bare clone by design.\n\nThe archived `docs/planning/P*_MULTIAGENT_EXECUTION_PLAN.md` files also reference\n`.claude/` paths. Those are historical records of how the work was executed and\nwere accurate when written, so they are left alone.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqiiDnCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAARpkQAINO+0/OwMixPeynzkSlkN2a\n5erMFKpDrVWbD9HtiBWwCBxaIgyM20nj+zhoCgxQ1V+Je/diA2rosWI+QygCJiF5\ne4jLf8aN61TN1n02SuisahM/qky97N/jtkP759PNHToykJ9OENjR3UMXqfQ3BVaZ\nuadx8pSYyEtpxbcgJHOmsDSVKPtyGiEwYuLrsCCdPFo3H9JcwGRpelQENEWuBq06\nxJhCTWK505FWlJaEEUN905dZuZWhw6zGsaenUcsE9jv4Vb3Yn8PeCwhz8u4LS8mw\n14Wn177U17b5pkLoKlb8jgO7xqQJgizy582h/fOx49I9txAqr9Z7RdMI+uIlc6xB\nNIGKNsAmcasKahwoFa+JKd5UCJ/npOp0wXbYauirg8fZXz4JL7+6R4TcN2QI2w3v\n3buwNOITYc8rVjAOkYa85ab+Y11ABt9YaE3+I7dUsbVNuN3J5HaKzJU5nl/2Kzco\nIMPDigb4Y2JzJO7uOYXhkgKfBWAWqFDXyzBeqQ84aW5twaYsO81GCI08MqEkNzxL\nFE9v9o/xVFDkG+bmX6iiBBBCxHh+kbKqUZ/F+tRutO7HdOKGaCI5ZBHH500AZmg6\nJytnpRkwvMkeXFdnStMI/V1RRIQRJiUq6TOFfq4dwAWdIFY/KO1x++ORBpDe+n+V\ny2zUe/ZutQ00evCTCWn2\n=Q1Je\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-22T22:21:27Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/snoodleboot-io/lavs-core/commit/eea01714bc01f4aaccd87142cc4a02bf7ceb401a","node_id":"C_kwDON50rGNoAKGVlYTAxNzE0YmMwMWY0YWFjY2Q4NzE0MmNjNGEwMmJmN2NlYjQwMWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/snoodleboot-io/lavs-core/commit/fac5b305641ec9072b27068a61a38656a50a4436","sha":"fac5b305641ec9072b27068a61a38656a50a4436","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/snoodleboot-io/lavs-core/commits/fac5b305641ec9072b27068a61a38656a50a4436"}],"sha":"eea01714bc01f4aaccd87142cc4a02bf7ceb401a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/snoodleboot-io/lavs-core/commits/eea01714bc01f4aaccd87142cc4a02bf7ceb401a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10266249?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/snoodleboot","id":10266249,"login":"snoodleboot","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMjY2MjQ5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/snoodleboot-io/lavs-core/commits/fac5b305641ec9072b27068a61a38656a50a4436/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-22T22:21:04Z","email":"John.aven.phd@gmail.com","name":"John Aven"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-22T22:21:04Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"bugfix(migration): schema-qualify the information_schema probes (#60) (#61)\n\n`information_schema` is not scoped to the current schema — on MySQL it spans\nevery visible database, on PostgreSQL and SQL Server every schema in the\ndatabase. The migration''s two introspection queries carried no `table_schema`\npredicate, so a `versions` table belonging to something else could answer them.\n\nAdds `Backend.current_schema_expression()`, following the same\ndefault-plus-override idiom as `init_schema` and `rename_table`: the default\n`current_schema()` serves DuckDB and PostgreSQL, MySQL overrides with\n`DATABASE()`, SQL Server with `SCHEMA_NAME()`. All three offending queries are\nnow constrained with it.\n\nThe third is `DatabaseManager._LIST_TABLES_SQL`, which has the identical defect\nand feeds `drop_tables`. That is a small extension beyond the issue text, taken\nbecause it is the same one-line mechanism; it is called only from integration\ntest teardown, never application code.\n\nThe severity is lower than first reported, and the test drafting is why. An\ninitial decoy test — a legacy-shaped table in another schema, against a fully\ninitialised database — passed with *and* without the fix. `_should_migrate`\nreads its row count from the current schema''s real `versions` table, and the\nrelational foreign keys mean rows there imply a non-empty `products`, so the\ndecoy can never tip the gate. The reachable failure is narrower: the probe\nreports a table the session cannot resolve, and the follow-up count raises. The\ntest now targets that, and was confirmed to fail without the fix with\n`UndefinedTable: relation \"versions\" does not exist`.\n\nMySQL gets no decoy test: its schemas are databases and the throwaway\ncontainer''s user has no CREATE DATABASE grant. Its `DATABASE()` expression stays\ncovered for non-regression by the three existing migration parity tests. The\nreasoning is recorded in the test file rather than left to be rediscovered.\n\nFull suite 548 passed (was 546); ruff and pyright clean.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"99c62921c653e55facd65c2c3c58f0ce5e793283","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/snoodleboot-io/lavs-core/git/trees/99c62921c653e55facd65c2c3c58f0ce5e793283"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/snoodleboot-io/lavs-core/git/commits/fac5b305641ec9072b27068a61a38656a50a4436","verification":{"payload":"tree 99c62921c653e55facd65c2c3c58f0ce5e793283\nparent 9c89483d2eb310f3088d6ef53688d782f6c19ad4\nauthor John Aven <John.aven.phd@gmail.com> 1787437264 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787437264 -0700\n\nbugfix(migration): schema-qualify the information_schema probes (#60) (#61)\n\n`information_schema` is not scoped to the current schema — on MySQL it spans\nevery visible database, on PostgreSQL and SQL Server every schema in the\ndatabase. The migration''s two introspection queries carried no `table_schema`\npredicate, so a `versions` table belonging to something else could answer them.\n\nAdds `Backend.current_schema_expression()`, following the same\ndefault-plus-override idiom as `init_schema` and `rename_table`: the default\n`current_schema()` serves DuckDB and PostgreSQL, MySQL overrides with\n`DATABASE()`, SQL Server with `SCHEMA_NAME()`. All three offending queries are\nnow constrained with it.\n\nThe third is `DatabaseManager._LIST_TABLES_SQL`, which has the identical defect\nand feeds `drop_tables`. That is a small extension beyond the issue text, taken\nbecause it is the same one-line mechanism; it is called only from integration\ntest teardown, never application code.\n\nThe severity is lower than first reported, and the test drafting is why. An\ninitial decoy test — a legacy-shaped table in another schema, against a fully\ninitialised database — passed with *and* without the fix. `_should_migrate`\nreads its row count from the current schema''s real `versions` table, and the\nrelational foreign keys mean rows there imply a non-empty `products`, so the\ndecoy can never tip the gate. The reachable failure is narrower: the probe\nreports a table the session cannot resolve, and the follow-up count raises. The\ntest now targets that, and was confirmed to fail without the fix with\n`UndefinedTable: relation \"versions\" does not exist`.\n\nMySQL gets no decoy test: its schemas are databases and the throwaway\ncontainer''s user has no CREATE DATABASE grant. Its `DATABASE()` expression stays\ncovered for non-regression by the three existing migration parity tests. The\nreasoning is recorded in the test file rather than left to be rediscovered.\n\nFull suite 548 passed (was 546); ruff and pyright clean.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqiiDQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA03sQAArW2C345Cvf+5+syShufHkU\nrNV7LJkcCZ6FalAzclMXkSroLB3W0uN8qQzv737ntVnYqL4vtxUjlNY6o/D5ty4P\nHkMfySM1eCsU2V7bYeH07meBLAWlrOy5fc04P3NlhilzB1PGv4piPKFNy1Fh4sAF\ngEc7Wnb7Uv4TW+j5/vcTJvJ406SldXGXPNJ3liDnv2/ky48BxHqjL/s93MfdzCXs\nIOY3j/28HQBCvZ07praKFnpho/0+wtnjQ1hNCZ/R6QcLa/3SFyjKSCejqF4OXqYx\ngfOEyfFuq2D+67hw9zYTEnAe0fO2/VdapJoqtRo7mRkRfJq7IuEo5QRBLDOoK9hJ\ndDEHCvwYtZyOxCeR+OmXXLZ4TIXnm5ojE8qWMupMeTqYoCkW/6kNRK4dfIPfPwDY\nv5XVGbTZZt69U5sGCcZIGrJwd5NcGqcxlTYh5ZUL3V00Lyp7efEr5Xj1PHImn/LT\niABHps+JO9ZKufLIUf5iLM3BdX6hOYFRlzUUNlnmWKUCXU0FwggPhTwFFP+rsiyg\nBaKt1qPUauN1zyhkiojFexmd9bsOGv8MrlZhsYCmHJAJI35tvHO75a+Zf1Ryv8oQ\nYHJZkfhuyLLXIc9tNzmbIUONoQHXVn35qKJfHakWaMEsAjA7CllNFN7fEXfTGANp\nlW5FLdgGAsO6LawuEFzM\n=gCA4\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-22T22:21:04Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/snoodleboot-io/lavs-core/commit/fac5b305641ec9072b27068a61a38656a50a4436","node_id":"C_kwDON50rGNoAKGZhYzViMzA1NjQxZWM5MDcyYjI3MDY4YTYxYTM4NjU2YTUwYTQ0MzY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/snoodleboot-io/lavs-core/commit/9c89483d2eb310f3088d6ef53688d782f6c19ad4","sha":"9c89483d2eb310f3088d6ef53688d782f6c19ad4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/snoodleboot-io/lavs-core/commits/9c89483d2eb310f3088d6ef53688d782f6c19ad4"}],"sha":"fac5b305641ec9072b27068a61a38656a50a4436","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/snoodleboot-io/lavs-core/commits/fac5b305641ec9072b27068a61a38656a50a4436"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10266249?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/snoodleboot","id":10266249,"login":"snoodleboot","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMjY2MjQ5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/snoodleboot-io/lavs-core/commits/9c89483d2eb310f3088d6ef53688d782f6c19ad4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-22T17:41:34Z","email":"John.aven.phd@gmail.com","name":"John Aven"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-22T17:41:34Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ci: gate frontend formatting with prettier, matching the backend (#58) (#59)\n\n* style(ui): apply prettier to the 6 files that had drifted (#58)\n\nMechanical reformat only — this applies the prettier config the project already\ndeclares, it does not choose a new style. Line-wrapping and nothing else: no\nlogic, no identifiers, no behaviour changed.\n\nSplit into its own commit so the CI step that follows is reviewable on its own.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci: gate frontend formatting with prettier, matching the backend (#58)\n\nThe backend has gated on `ruff format --check` since v1; the frontend did not.\n#57 added typecheck, lint, test and build for the Constellation UI but skipped\n`pnpm format:check`, because it was failing on 6 files at the time and wiring it\nwould have either reddened the new gate or buried a reformat inside a CI change.\n\nThose files are normalised in the preceding commit, so the gate can now be added\ncleanly. The step sits after lint, mirroring the backend job''s ordering.\n\nAlso drops the workflow comment claiming `format:check` is deliberately absent —\nthat is no longer true. The comment now documents only the Playwright e2e\nexclusion, which still holds: e2e needs browser downloads and a live server, so\nit belongs in its own job rather than the PR gate.\n\nAll five gates verified from a CI-equivalent run: typecheck, lint, format:check,\ntest (111 passed), build. This closes the last known gate difference between the\ntwo halves of the repo.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5b1a3421393a95acade1c9e568014bb91b1c3b38","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/snoodleboot-io/lavs-core/git/trees/5b1a3421393a95acade1c9e568014bb91b1c3b38"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/snoodleboot-io/lavs-core/git/commits/9c89483d2eb310f3088d6ef53688d782f6c19ad4","verification":{"payload":"tree 5b1a3421393a95acade1c9e568014bb91b1c3b38\nparent 44ecb808a86a582dd23ec4dbe29c31e1fdb95d13\nauthor John Aven <John.aven.phd@gmail.com> 1787420494 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787420494 -0700\n\nci: gate frontend formatting with prettier, matching the backend (#58) (#59)\n\n* style(ui): apply prettier to the 6 files that had drifted (#58)\n\nMechanical reformat only — this applies the prettier config the project already\ndeclares, it does not choose a new style. Line-wrapping and nothing else: no\nlogic, no identifiers, no behaviour changed.\n\nSplit into its own commit so the CI step that follows is reviewable on its own.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci: gate frontend formatting with prettier, matching the backend (#58)\n\nThe backend has gated on `ruff format --check` since v1; the frontend did not.\n#57 added typecheck, lint, test and build for the Constellation UI but skipped\n`pnpm format:check`, because it was failing on 6 files at the time and wiring it\nwould have either reddened the new gate or buried a reformat inside a CI change.\n\nThose files are normalised in the preceding commit, so the gate can now be added\ncleanly. The step sits after lint, mirroring the backend job''s ordering.\n\nAlso drops the workflow comment claiming `format:check` is deliberately absent —\nthat is no longer true. The comment now documents only the Playwright e2e\nexclusion, which still holds: e2e needs browser downloads and a live server, so\nit belongs in its own job rather than the PR gate.\n\nAll five gates verified from a CI-equivalent run: typecheck, lint, format:check,\ntest (111 passed), build. This closes the last known gate difference between the\ntwo halves of the repo.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqid9OCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAixkQAEC+GejOSSLbZFVFP8ljz/qk\nJikZt4EhpVgAnFeIvK8hMVyKmne0ukqA7p86MNcpXp6xyehw0QK3pFyzlBfzXVxg\n6luHvZDQNcsv1FbSfwOtxfd9uazoYyMN2nmfxjPpMxqrTrcintjRs3FhO82ZunhC\nBpNdoTFDMm4eOkVgR1ZDsT6UvICJSbazr1oYIi1RUGLik2VY7KRx3l5zsZA90bIP\nOWri7yo6/8qNenOO/u00/TKPzc6hvlmt6ZcC2i3svZNSiLQCX2ONzdBQ/hQfJ7mz\nwUQ/JbduMxtxpndSAX7X7zAtZLqsQBC3j/QjjfvguYuwh7Dyljs4CwgITJTbxBwC\nrabGE2fTvr6ewF3ZkjN4wIP0KeJV+o/ynjuWzfWtxzgpfBggsZLD+C1XnOGWmx69\n+LwKCI8w5NL25F01cyG7W0MJt8d5onAdmZkqoE6QjaG7oCymASJPhYFuJ8mlct/z\nOYGZEaShhW8j22QSbCvTtdKRZv6fmZzyNSWX/hzoEyDiSFLWMVCl6Xzs/8s0S+Ke\nhwVctEtIJPM+AxiKOYlRLLBcyBeYj7IiSUlMNYxI/K59FiQuu9L2fWFvR+iO5lvA\n3ouIc7XO8RR6NqNaUf643RFLuO5angsL+hOhpw9H9S14mKEjFsj8FNJQM+kuANCy\nabYhxYlkVJ++1bGChIGn\n=v+/b\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-22T17:41:35Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/snoodleboot-io/lavs-core/commit/9c89483d2eb310f3088d6ef53688d782f6c19ad4","node_id":"C_kwDON50rGNoAKDljODk0ODNkMmViMzEwZjMwODhkNmVmNTM2ODhkNzgyZjZjMTlhZDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/snoodleboot-io/lavs-core/commit/44ecb808a86a582dd23ec4dbe29c31e1fdb95d13","sha":"44ecb808a86a582dd23ec4dbe29c31e1fdb95d13","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/snoodleboot-io/lavs-core/commits/44ecb808a86a582dd23ec4dbe29c31e1fdb95d13"}],"sha":"9c89483d2eb310f3088d6ef53688d782f6c19ad4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/snoodleboot-io/lavs-core/commits/9c89483d2eb310f3088d6ef53688d782f6c19ad4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10266249?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/snoodleboot","id":10266249,"login":"snoodleboot","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMjY2MjQ5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/snoodleboot-io/lavs-core/commits/44ecb808a86a582dd23ec4dbe29c31e1fdb95d13/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-22T05:07:26Z","email":"John.aven.phd@gmail.com","name":"John Aven"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-22T05:07:26Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ci: gate the Constellation UI — and recover the src/lib source directory it was hiding (#56) (#57)\n\n* ci: gate the Constellation UI on tests, types, lint and build (#56)\n\nThe workflow had exactly one frontend job — `frontend-audit`, running only\n`pnpm audit --prod`. Nothing ran the UI''s tests, types, lint or build, so the\nwhole P5 Constellation UI was ungated: 25 test files (111 tests) never executed,\nand a change that broke the build or the types still landed on a green CI. The\nbackend meanwhile carries 546 enforced tests plus multi-backend parity that\ncannot be skipped.\n\nAdds a `frontend-test` job running typecheck → lint → test → build, with the\npnpm store cached on `frontend/ui/pnpm-lock.yaml`. All four gates already pass,\nso this is wiring, not repair.\n\nVerified from the CI-equivalent state rather than the local dev tree: the first\n`--frozen-lockfile` install refused to run because `node_modules` had drifted\nfrom the lockfile, so it was re-run with `CI=true` to purge and reinstall\nexactly as Actions does, and all four gates re-run on that clean tree — 111\ntests passed, build 394 modules in 3.4s. That step mattered, because pnpm 10\nignores build scripts for `esbuild` and `msw`, and the build could plausibly\nhave failed on a fresh install while passing on the existing tree.\n\n`pnpm format:check` is deliberately excluded: it currently fails on 6 files, so\nwiring it would either redden the gate or force a formatting-churn commit across\nsource. Playwright e2e is excluded too — it needs browser downloads and a live\nserver, so it belongs in its own job rather than the PR gate. Both exclusions\nare recorded in the workflow itself.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(repo): stop .gitignore swallowing the UI''s src/lib source directory\n\nThe new frontend CI gate immediately caught something the repo had been hiding:\n`frontend/ui/src/lib/` was never committed. `tsc` failed in CI with 11 ×\n`TS2307: Cannot find module ''@/lib''`, while passing locally, because the files\nexist on developer machines and nowhere else.\n\nThe cause is `.gitignore`''s `lib/` entry, inherited from the stock Python\npackaging template where it means distutils output at the repo root. Left\nunanchored, a bare `lib/` matches at *any* depth — so it silently swallowed the\nUI''s own source directory. Auditing what that rule actually excluded across the\nwhole repo turned up exactly one thing: `frontend/ui/src/lib/`. It was doing no\nuseful work and only causing harm.\n\n`lib/` and `lib64/` are now anchored to the repo root, with a comment recording\nwhy, and the 7 orphaned files are committed:\n\n  index.ts  palette.ts  query-fn.ts  query-keys.ts  semver.ts\n  query-keys.test.ts  semver.test.ts\n\n`index.ts` is the barrel that `@/lib` resolves to, so without it a clean clone\ncould not type-check or build the frontend at all. Two of the seven are test\nfiles, so 10 of the suite''s 111 tests were likewise running only on developer\nmachines.\n\nAnchoring was verified not to un-ignore anything else in the repo.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c63e9a53bdfaa991e609550db08c74177d97f9d8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/snoodleboot-io/lavs-core/git/trees/c63e9a53bdfaa991e609550db08c74177d97f9d8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/snoodleboot-io/lavs-core/git/commits/44ecb808a86a582dd23ec4dbe29c31e1fdb95d13","verification":{"payload":"tree c63e9a53bdfaa991e609550db08c74177d97f9d8\nparent aa4ac3f46aec10cb23117100ffbacb88acb00635\nauthor John Aven <John.aven.phd@gmail.com> 1787375246 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787375246 -0700\n\nci: gate the Constellation UI — and recover the src/lib source directory it was hiding (#56) (#57)\n\n* ci: gate the Constellation UI on tests, types, lint and build (#56)\n\nThe workflow had exactly one frontend job — `frontend-audit`, running only\n`pnpm audit --prod`. Nothing ran the UI''s tests, types, lint or build, so the\nwhole P5 Constellation UI was ungated: 25 test files (111 tests) never executed,\nand a change that broke the build or the types still landed on a green CI. The\nbackend meanwhile carries 546 enforced tests plus multi-backend parity that\ncannot be skipped.\n\nAdds a `frontend-test` job running typecheck → lint → test → build, with the\npnpm store cached on `frontend/ui/pnpm-lock.yaml`. All four gates already pass,\nso this is wiring, not repair.\n\nVerified from the CI-equivalent state rather than the local dev tree: the first\n`--frozen-lockfile` install refused to run because `node_modules` had drifted\nfrom the lockfile, so it was re-run with `CI=true` to purge and reinstall\nexactly as Actions does, and all four gates re-run on that clean tree — 111\ntests passed, build 394 modules in 3.4s. That step mattered, because pnpm 10\nignores build scripts for `esbuild` and `msw`, and the build could plausibly\nhave failed on a fresh install while passing on the existing tree.\n\n`pnpm format:check` is deliberately excluded: it currently fails on 6 files, so\nwiring it would either redden the gate or force a formatting-churn commit across\nsource. Playwright e2e is excluded too — it needs browser downloads and a live\nserver, so it belongs in its own job rather than the PR gate. Both exclusions\nare recorded in the workflow itself.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(repo): stop .gitignore swallowing the UI''s src/lib source directory\n\nThe new frontend CI gate immediately caught something the repo had been hiding:\n`frontend/ui/src/lib/` was never committed. `tsc` failed in CI with 11 ×\n`TS2307: Cannot find module ''@/lib''`, while passing locally, because the files\nexist on developer machines and nowhere else.\n\nThe cause is `.gitignore`''s `lib/` entry, inherited from the stock Python\npackaging template where it means distutils output at the repo root. Left\nunanchored, a bare `lib/` matches at *any* depth — so it silently swallowed the\nUI''s own source directory. Auditing what that rule actually excluded across the\nwhole repo turned up exactly one thing: `frontend/ui/src/lib/`. It was doing no\nuseful work and only causing harm.\n\n`lib/` and `lib64/` are now anchored to the repo root, with a comment recording\nwhy, and the 7 orphaned files are committed:\n\n  index.ts  palette.ts  query-fn.ts  query-keys.ts  semver.ts\n  query-keys.test.ts  semver.test.ts\n\n`index.ts` is the barrel that `@/lib` resolves to, so without it a clean clone\ncould not type-check or build the frontend at all. Two of the seven are test\nfiles, so 10 of the suite''s 111 tests were likewise running only on developer\nmachines.\n\nAnchoring was verified not to un-ignore anything else in the repo.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqiS6OCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAvc8QAJOhLupq1fG8EMzrOsPdWVCg\n91ZRB0Glkzr8p4xcIdVgkX9GSMiFbd23zmzLujZR1j9Jz4UupeJFmxJRUOWnsnCO\nXxM8/IXN7tFOfzbW/px87hmAwMTQJYXlUFbByVqIEUK3y64KHYFDGegTICla2aMj\n38F0KxSW7tX+452S/XzTe85ALbdjjfs6DnCSJn/AvC3u/eeJKHx0wnjYtR6l8iZL\nr0iPzV8Y3V+fKzjWT0hrkaTrTErUPrdPV21B6tdgHk/kfrG0luWOliWmyY6bnB9C\nQ69Gx5Ne2t3GyHfKKvwAId5JmNwI8hZnlsWo+TY9VyR8ZTJphf99s4BmSeqlsqnQ\nErwr25c3nYxLIRIqpBAEG9vXCrbeJ8yHCo+XxNyJcEU+EhQsIHUHxixlSC/2uEnk\nj7KOIyFEyaoUQ6jKGNt/6j1qchqXPJ2uvzOUN7zDIecrHgBVmGHAbPuYNeVbdAKU\nXRwlv16rhqBwGbboQJk7Uv1llqBMWJFZasm+425YUbntNQrAN+katqwsKG4v7GS9\npxhXmyMtLmOtLirOVwyX3Dy9y4/922egJXudwluHM0quZWY2D6Sm8JQ72ONFLFbK\nn6wE6wQdzPquGQCFtDQcThXT7zKFewSrApRJpg6cU5n+BUeB7PDjFmYB6gNYA3Xd\nRfo29hwgbv5yaJRhdf0d\n=5SgV\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-22T05:07:26Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/snoodleboot-io/lavs-core/commit/44ecb808a86a582dd23ec4dbe29c31e1fdb95d13","node_id":"C_kwDON50rGNoAKDQ0ZWNiODA4YTg2YTU4MmRkMjNlYzRkYmUyOWMzMWUxZmRiOTVkMTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/snoodleboot-io/lavs-core/commit/aa4ac3f46aec10cb23117100ffbacb88acb00635","sha":"aa4ac3f46aec10cb23117100ffbacb88acb00635","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/snoodleboot-io/lavs-core/commits/aa4ac3f46aec10cb23117100ffbacb88acb00635"}],"sha":"44ecb808a86a582dd23ec4dbe29c31e1fdb95d13","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/snoodleboot-io/lavs-core/commits/44ecb808a86a582dd23ec4dbe29c31e1fdb95d13"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10266249?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/snoodleboot","id":10266249,"login":"snoodleboot","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMjY2MjQ5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/snoodleboot-io/lavs-core/commits/aa4ac3f46aec10cb23117100ffbacb88acb00635/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-22T05:07:13Z","email":"John.aven.phd@gmail.com","name":"John Aven"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-22T05:07:13Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"bugfix(migration): make the flat→relational migration portable across all four backends (#54) (#55)\n\n`FlatToRelationalMigration` runs unconditionally on every boot, for every\nbackend, but predated MySQL (#48) and SQL Server (#52) and was only ever tested\non DuckDB. Two of its steps emitted SQL that those dialects reject.\n\n* Archive step — `ALTER TABLE … RENAME TO` is not valid T-SQL. The rename moves\n  onto the `Backend` seam as `rename_table`, using this file''s existing\n  default-plus-override idiom (as `init_schema` already does): the ANSI form is\n  the default, and `MssqlBackend` overrides it with `sp_rename`. Because\n  `sp_rename` takes its arguments as values rather than identifiers, that\n  override binds them as parameters instead of interpolating.\n\n* Rebuild step — `DatabaseManager.create_tables_on` hardcodes `duckdb/ddl.sql`,\n  so the post-archive rebuild ran DuckDB DDL on whatever backend was live. It\n  now calls the running backend''s own `init_schema`, which is already guarded\n  (`IF NOT EXISTS` / `IF OBJECT_ID`) and so is a safe no-op over existing tables.\n\nBoth were reproduced before being fixed, by reverting each change and watching\nthe new parity tests fail: SQL Server gave `Incorrect syntax near ''RENAME''` and\n`Incorrect syntax near the keyword ''IF''`, MySQL rejected the unbounded\n`VARCHAR`. PostgreSQL passes either way — DuckDB''s DDL happens to be\nPG-compatible — which is why nothing surfaced this until the matrix widened.\n\n`tests/backends/test_migration_parity.py` drives the real migration against real\nPostgreSQL, MySQL and SQL Server containers, retiring the last unconditional\nboot-path code with no parity coverage. ROADMAP §6 is closed out: the one-shot\nmigration was decided and shipped, not still open.\n\nFull suite 546 passed (was 543); ruff and pyright clean.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"59b85ee31191b1eabb9a1280c933bab41d15b4b0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/snoodleboot-io/lavs-core/git/trees/59b85ee31191b1eabb9a1280c933bab41d15b4b0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/snoodleboot-io/lavs-core/git/commits/aa4ac3f46aec10cb23117100ffbacb88acb00635","verification":{"payload":"tree 59b85ee31191b1eabb9a1280c933bab41d15b4b0\nparent 82503812417fa848936f3decca53a621e4e3e089\nauthor John Aven <John.aven.phd@gmail.com> 1787375233 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787375233 -0700\n\nbugfix(migration): make the flat→relational migration portable across all four backends (#54) (#55)\n\n`FlatToRelationalMigration` runs unconditionally on every boot, for every\nbackend, but predated MySQL (#48) and SQL Server (#52) and was only ever tested\non DuckDB. Two of its steps emitted SQL that those dialects reject.\n\n* Archive step — `ALTER TABLE … RENAME TO` is not valid T-SQL. The rename moves\n  onto the `Backend` seam as `rename_table`, using this file''s existing\n  default-plus-override idiom (as `init_schema` already does): the ANSI form is\n  the default, and `MssqlBackend` overrides it with `sp_rename`. Because\n  `sp_rename` takes its arguments as values rather than identifiers, that\n  override binds them as parameters instead of interpolating.\n\n* Rebuild step — `DatabaseManager.create_tables_on` hardcodes `duckdb/ddl.sql`,\n  so the post-archive rebuild ran DuckDB DDL on whatever backend was live. It\n  now calls the running backend''s own `init_schema`, which is already guarded\n  (`IF NOT EXISTS` / `IF OBJECT_ID`) and so is a safe no-op over existing tables.\n\nBoth were reproduced before being fixed, by reverting each change and watching\nthe new parity tests fail: SQL Server gave `Incorrect syntax near ''RENAME''` and\n`Incorrect syntax near the keyword ''IF''`, MySQL rejected the unbounded\n`VARCHAR`. PostgreSQL passes either way — DuckDB''s DDL happens to be\nPG-compatible — which is why nothing surfaced this until the matrix widened.\n\n`tests/backends/test_migration_parity.py` drives the real migration against real\nPostgreSQL, MySQL and SQL Server containers, retiring the last unconditional\nboot-path code with no parity coverage. ROADMAP §6 is closed out: the one-shot\nmigration was decided and shipped, not still open.\n\nFull suite 546 passed (was 543); ruff and pyright clean.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqiS6BCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjS8QAK+Csld16tl1p4Slk/j4bg2x\n0eb6Xgl8zC4Zm6N9dTJPWhHGz3B9sNDLTnzAwJsodaLjHJLvjeLbMUSrgwUQ4Ocu\nc0BuWh1+RulaKvbT8b+/a05rsj8oDN220gnUY+zlabzsV0EaiT20Kref1s7m9z+T\nzCwAbDPLTCReRAW4mUl7xZmbX8qNDBAOE0LKrBhvQAalCsHPFuP7AVXt0e0W2NYW\nzGij6ZkEPULCRca91HGXleOc/Eb6/+0X2topMkf1QVvxnICNuOzI08pm7we4h8+i\nglSEjnrTOn+pmseHdDyV2U2GdpL5Zo9+jHKgDQBAVNlUUJb7Sy7TtLwFRfSzsul1\n7at8po8v8hGijyH6nUbDeIjD5clw7y51EHXcDUC8P+Gfmuom04Bx/JlKHlcJptn/\n1uYHU4AeSf6VRmeE7AFcqw15TI/tGbWq9cVLXYtR6L9Edr7BIq5Xua+53lsVKQ1M\nxaIITSRYqZmzzDCR1ex38tsy8rvhwIqShDSQgmFp+cTMTC+UBGAtpOKGTCz29mrL\nMiPqxXOmxX9LX7joIHSC1mdLbbP2SecA+h5LSLObqiTCDw18Oymh//CTeOgolCaq\n7rwIuUmsuCBsa10zmAdge9zH8Iys5mzXArE6SfV1JDeixWd1FZ17nWtZZFOLSb5X\nkICLqFKdXERVeiqb8CQM\n=wmk2\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-22T05:07:14Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/snoodleboot-io/lavs-core/commit/aa4ac3f46aec10cb23117100ffbacb88acb00635","node_id":"C_kwDON50rGNoAKGFhNGFjM2Y0NmFlYzEwY2IyMzExNzEwMGZmYmFjYjg4YWNiMDA2MzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/snoodleboot-io/lavs-core/commit/82503812417fa848936f3decca53a621e4e3e089","sha":"82503812417fa848936f3decca53a621e4e3e089","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/snoodleboot-io/lavs-core/commits/82503812417fa848936f3decca53a621e4e3e089"}],"sha":"aa4ac3f46aec10cb23117100ffbacb88acb00635","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/snoodleboot-io/lavs-core/commits/aa4ac3f46aec10cb23117100ffbacb88acb00635"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10266249?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/snoodleboot","id":10266249,"login":"snoodleboot","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMjY2MjQ5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/snoodleboot","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/snoodleboot-io/lavs-core/commits/82503812417fa848936f3decca53a621e4e3e089/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T03:33:03Z","email":"John.aven.phd@gmail.com","name":"John Aven"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T03:33:03Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(persistence): SQL Server backend — completes the multi-DB matrix (#51) (#52)\n\nFourth dialect behind the Backend interface, mirroring MySqlBackend:\n- MssqlBackend (pymssql, PYFORMAT %s, autocommit, split-statement init_schema)\n- PyMssqlConnection adapter (cursor-per-execute; params bound, never formatted)\n- app/database/mssql/ddl.sql (T-SQL: DATETIME2 not the rowversion TIMESTAMP;\n  IF OBJECT_ID(...) IS NULL idempotent creates; NVARCHAR(MAX); table-level FKs)\n- BackendKind.MSSQL + LAVS_MSSQL_* settings + additive registration (DuckDB\n  stays default)\n\nAdding SQL Server exposed two latent portability assumptions in the SHARED\nquery layer, now fixed dialect-portably (behavior-preserving, all backends green):\n- new StatementDialect seam (ANSI identity / TSQL rewrites trailing LIMIT n →\n  SELECT TOP n) — value-safe, only the integer literal moves\n- rollback_version_query: row-value predicate (a,b,c) < (?,?,?) → expanded\n  lexicographic OR (SQL Server has no row constructor). Verified equivalent;\n  9 params map position-for-position.\n\nNew runtime dep: pymssql>=2.3 (2.3.13; manylinux wheel, no system libs). Exit\ncriterion met — same parity suite green against a live mssql:2022 testcontainer\n(8 tests, no skips). 518 → 543 tests. Gates A/B PASS; ruff/format/pyright clean.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ae8e51d5a140acd0ddac90bd4dc7b1c649c2e587","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/snoodleboot-io/lavs-core/git/trees/ae8e51d5a140acd0ddac90bd4dc7b1c649c2e587"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/snoodleboot-io/lavs-core/git/commits/82503812417fa848936f3decca53a621e4e3e089","verification":{"payload":"tree ae8e51d5a140acd0ddac90bd4dc7b1c649c2e587\nparent 3bed89228de3269dd6379b091b7eb3830826ce12\nauthor John Aven <John.aven.phd@gmail.com> 1786851183 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786851183 +0000\n\nfeat(persistence): SQL Server backend — completes the multi-DB matrix (#51) (#52)\n\nFourth dialect behind the Backend interface, mirroring MySqlBackend:\n- MssqlBackend (pymssql, PYFORMAT %s, autocommit, split-statement init_schema)\n- PyMssqlConnection adapter (cursor-per-execute; params bound, never formatted)\n- app/database/mssql/ddl.sql (T-SQL: DATETIME2 not the rowversion TIMESTAMP;\n  IF OBJECT_ID(...) IS NULL idempotent creates; NVARCHAR(MAX); table-level FKs)\n- BackendKind.MSSQL + LAVS_MSSQL_* settings + additive registration (DuckDB\n  stays default)\n\nAdding SQL Server exposed two latent portability assumptions in the SHARED\nquery layer, now fixed dialect-portably (behavior-preserving, all backends green):\n- new StatementDialect seam (ANSI identity / TSQL rewrites trailing LIMIT n →\n  SELECT TOP n) — value-safe, only the integer literal moves\n- rollback_version_query: row-value predicate (a,b,c) < (?,?,?) → expanded\n  lexicographic OR (SQL Server has no row constructor). Verified equivalent;\n  9 params map position-for-position.\n\nNew runtime dep: pymssql>=2.3 (2.3.13; manylinux wheel, no system libs). Exit\ncriterion met — same parity suite green against a live mssql:2022 testcontainer\n(8 tests, no skips). 518 → 543 tests. Gates A/B PASS; ruff/format/pyright clean.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqgS9vCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAKMkQADvhoWoF7go2zImOtE1D4Qoc\nUL/Fq7Kty39POo95DrA1/dFBYNR8/Pl+lOGAq0b2e4w1B5EYhAPMmaJTG9XK+2/M\n+jmFoE4Jy8nXSANM31vUdbWq2AOMUUhHSJiq98ofRhEpScoCEEMts2M/x4he0vnc\n/8Op43EELB7wuwXVcywrpOukUAH5kS2u8hilnthtwTiEVw2Ax9eOp6f/tIkNHjcf\nG0E0PFrxTICPlhHUtxwT1TqPzr/T3hTmrzdSS0JR5Q+qCZib60BChaoShRmkwVG0\nrEZF3BqIUL1znU1ivCfPO2wh8kmx+CtNzsr6Bf2ntmcJ3q/M6MlFzg3XsWvn+DWj\nmesW+X8przNhJioswJjCn2Xc1JV1N3F5mHJ+d/pgVw01Y0q6IgQAvHY2l4iwIhKF\n4tbBSTLbaqkyTUPdNp39kYCylcZ4cT0wrsiSPYkKQlpNjWeJb5GoMRJUv6U+xBhs\n4oIuWEy3myjErhHfgUgajzzrhnI83Pcoqbs1nlRhYi6MLJ1BUQYT9xEOXpKa3iT8\n6RDEgRAwsRg+oawzGOafADfnrWHPOCHBT+sxGnWJMebpguOmEm5P7k4TdB2S/utC\nauzLnigi0qbM2z7/VFVtBdG0B83UFBGSC0aopfMUr6jzPRf0cPyofj3I3ICJJ233\n3q8bGxtwGrK6FUmxBczp\n=yfsn\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-16T03:33:04Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.