":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/snoodleboot-io/lavs-core/commits/0fa16047edfec6144b1a8e7d5c0019d8f2e6e23b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-15T23:07:43Z","email":"John.aven.phd@gmail.com","name":"John Aven"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-15T23:07:43Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"bugfix: make /ready + /health async so probes don''t race the shared DuckDB conn (#45) (#46)\n\nValidated ROADMAP §6: under concurrent load the async resource API is\nevent-loop-serialized and safe (200 concurrent writes, 0 errors, no\ncorruption), but the SYNC /ready handler runs in the threadpool and touches\nthe single shared DuckDBPyConnection from another thread — racing its cursor\nand raising _duckdb.InvalidInputException (~2% spurious 503 at 64-way).\n\nDeclaring /ready (and /health) async moves their DB touch onto the event\nloop, serialized with all other access. Re-probed: /ready x500 @96 workers →\n0 failures, 0 races (was 4x503 + InvalidInputException). ROADMAP §6 updated\nwith the validated result.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8690415ba4dc0e5bdcd21ca6f11f1335b60cb701","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/snoodleboot-io/lavs-core/git/trees/8690415ba4dc0e5bdcd21ca6f11f1335b60cb701"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/snoodleboot-io/lavs-core/git/commits/0fa16047edfec6144b1a8e7d5c0019d8f2e6e23b","verification":{"payload":"tree 8690415ba4dc0e5bdcd21ca6f11f1335b60cb701\nparent c99996dd8cba519f46ac64d487ebaf65b6a7cd2d\nauthor John Aven <John.aven.phd@gmail.com> 1786835263 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786835263 +0000\n\nbugfix: make /ready + /health async so probes don''t race the shared DuckDB conn (#45) (#46)\n\nValidated ROADMAP §6: under concurrent load the async resource API is\nevent-loop-serialized and safe (200 concurrent writes, 0 errors, no\ncorruption), but the SYNC /ready handler runs in the threadpool and touches\nthe single shared DuckDBPyConnection from another thread — racing its cursor\nand raising _duckdb.InvalidInputException (~2% spurious 503 at 64-way).\n\nDeclaring /ready (and /health) async moves their DB touch onto the event\nloop, serialized with all other access. Re-probed: /ready x500 @96 workers →\n0 failures, 0 races (was 4x503 + InvalidInputException). ROADMAP §6 updated\nwith the validated result.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqgPE/CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA274QAHNfMIWypWp69D+8CCHdsCeB\nabOlPz0a28cKVaYqgloIySNMgv4bscsI1xcoXf2r9w3SVqFWIB7sVr2DXNKQZKFt\nJMBLo7YmoYRZhDWpfMu7V1z2nvpm4DFjIcUgS1+h23Oci6oBoDsVQ0gLDE6cgnkx\n80hjNlmg5vsFo3S+YHGLNRmiavplk35xusYUxd4RwBSXM1h9S539OZJxywKibZV3\ni+mlJCS6nm069LYsGj5ZUbKe33kFYM+O+yNX2ZFyAOPFaAdAJdnPHqXGMTaQ2QMl\nW6x+nFNPcti9bIMQtPsd+lfij0fvOprWLTLZJKNx8IIRqUn/r6SW3/lVooz4GUN5\noZ5mhbUn0DhqcHLMCUMBfCbnHO26EWjefyXBTh0bEeMfqls5RrjnBtTOEmundXwY\n+ASjD8jf+gtCteToJYmTO3tlxbNsbsWlSsfK1/FFSJ6QNc7p32WcijQtPGTXs7SX\nL6GUd+LZBAOzWGhQw0Ggh/sTR/o42iazYGooO3JNwuRjNdqf+hDzzHsWJZ9w/Lfs\nXKwfJNMxFPgYNf+wq75mruoqfrtDB/HP02vkBYWXsNNn3oSRruzTQSR3zAsWSHQ9\nesoqi0pK1kViWYNrlo6OW2Tj4tfnGRacUGhpITQtiXuTELTl9D+0HtcF4rds7LQE\nVJqwQAT8ZhhC4tLt84bV\n=y9O3\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-15T23:07:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/r